This resume project was conceived and executed in a matter of minutes. The objective was to leverage AI to aggregate my professional footprint from across the web and synthesize it into a coherent resume based on a few minor design specifications.

The requested output was a consolidated Markdown file and a single-page static HTML file utilizing CDNs for external resources. After iterating through several layouts in my own HackMicro web editor for light prototyping web projects, I finalized a design that met my requirements.

### The Deployment Pipeline

I established a GitHub repository titled `resume` and uploaded the final `index.html`. While I typically manage my own infrastructure, having overseen over 600 sites and 15 VPS servers over the last decade, I decided to experiment with the DigitalOcean App Platform.

The integration was seamless. By connecting the repository to the App Platform, I established a continuous deployment pipeline that automatically reflects changes pushed to the repo. While the initial deployment generated a generic DigitalOcean subdomain, the configuration of my existing `raykooyenga.com` domain allowed for a quick CNAME adjustment.

### Results and Reflections

Within minutes, I had successfully moved from a conceptual prompt to a live, hosted resume served at:  
[resume.raykooyenga.com](https://resume.raykooyenga.com)

From a non technical perspective, this might appear to be an over-engineered solution for a simple document. However, compared to traditional manual workflows, this represents a significant optimization. The true overengineered solution would be if it continually updates itself by sourcing changes in data sources. I elected not to go that route, yet.

As a final touch, I dictated this summary via voice-to-text to OpenAI, requesting a refined Markdown output to document the process. If only every technical endeavor offered this level of efficiency and enjoyment.

